## Context

Ticket 1489 (closed, PR #2352) ran `/paper <data paper> published` on host
doudou, inspection only, for the RDJHSS data paper (DOI 10.52024/fn48qf66).
Its log lists six steps the agent needed that
`skills/paper/references/published.md` lacks. The author ruled on 2026-11-10
(decision A, relayed by the interface session): a ticket for the six steps,
worked by a coder; the paper's own open rows are ticket 1505.

The six, from the 1489 log (21:55Z):

- (a) hash-compare the hosted file and the landing-page PDF against the mail
  attachment (the papers directory's `AGENTS.md` demands it; the checklist
  says only "hash both");
- (b) check the HAL deposit is the version of record publicly, not only that
  a PUT was sent (a PUT in moderation does not show);
- (c) reconcile title and page range across bib, landing page and HAL;
- (d) the event date is the publisher's (publication mail / landing page),
  not the day `/paper` is invoked: reconcile it before writing any register;
- (e) recognise a re-run on a partly done event: inspect each row's state
  first, redo only what is not done;
- (f) say how to read the roadmap row when the roadmap is an odt.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] `skills/paper/references/published.md` carries (a)-(f), each placed at
  the step it belongs to; `skills/paper/SKILL.md` changes only for a step
  that cannot live in the reference, with the reason in the commit message
- [ ] No test asserts the wording of skill text
- [ ] gaze REVIEWED on the branch head; the author lands the request
